WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.930
- [Narrator] In 2019, this
new BMW marked the start

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.577
of a new production in a car
plants in Western Russia.

00:00:07.577 --> 00:00:08.730
(audience applaud)

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.960
Today, it is Chinese cars
coming off the assembly line.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.630
The factory produced tens
of thousands of vehicles

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:19.080
including Ford trucks, German BMWs,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.870
and South Korean Hyundais every year

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.690
until Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.660
As international sanctions
prompted foreign automakers

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.200
to leave the country, Chinese
brands filled the void,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.270
making billions of dollars.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.820
- Car makers who have been struggling

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.560
in the domestic market in China,

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.800
they're finding an opportunistic
moment when it comes

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.120
to the Russian market.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.400
- [Narrator] Here's how Chinese
car makers are profiting

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.250
from the Western corporate
exodus and what it means

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:48.993
for Russia's auto markets.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.210
Car making is one of
Russia's main industries.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.570
It employed some 300,000 people directly

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.370
and produced vehicles and parts worth

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.640
about $42 billion in 2020.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.720
- The first Renault created
for the Russian market.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.090
- [Narrator] Foreign
automakers opened factories

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.340
and partnered with local brands,

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.930
pushing Russia into the ranks

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.480
of the world's top car producers,

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.420
and Russians eagerly embraced foreign cars

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.390
with Japanese, Korean, and European brands

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:24.033
dominating the market for years.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:24.960
(tank fires)

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.040
But Moscow's invasion of
Ukraine hit the industry hard.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.590
Western sanctions cut off Russia's access

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.530
to global supply chains
for essential parts

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.210
such as computer chips,

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.000
prompting many foreign
brands to halt production

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.070
or withdraw from the country.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:44.340
Soaring inflation and
uncertainty contributed

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.763
to a dramatic drop in car
sales in the country last year.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.750
But assembly lines didn't
stay idle for long.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:55.740
Demands started to pick up
as Chinese brands stepped in.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.330
Car dealerships across Russia

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:59.970
started reopening under new brands.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.670
For example, this showroom outside Moscow

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:06.390
changed from Nissan to Kaiyi from China.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.080
Russian buyers became more
familiar with Chinese cars.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.840
Chinese SUVs have even been spotted

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.180
in the Kremlin's motorcades.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:19.200
By mid 2023, the list of the
10 most popular car brands

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.410
in Russia looked very
different to before the war.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.420
Six of them were Chinese.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:27.150
This year, Russia became
the number one buyer

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:30.900
of Chinese vehicles,
spending some $6 billion

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.540
in the first four months of 2023,

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:37.650
helping China to become the
world's largest auto exporter.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.830
- The exports to Russia have
got an outsize importance,

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.140
especially for the car
makers who have struggled

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.900
to pivot to a successful EV strategy.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.680
Within China, the sales of
petroleum-powered vehicles

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.680
have dropped, so they now
have some excess capacity

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.880
and Russia presents a good
opportunity for these car makers.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.790
- [Narrator] But Russia's
markets also poses challenges.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.490
- As Chinese car brands
become more mature,

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.670
I think a lot of them are
seriously considering the prospect

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:09.450
of one day become the world's
biggest auto manufacturer.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.120
And in the grand scheme of things,

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.970
Russia may not be a big consideration

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.220
for them because of the constraints

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.290
in this market at present.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.750
- [Narrator] Chinese
automakers are also not immune

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.900
to the bad publicity that
comes with working in Russia.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.390
In June, in a symbolic gesture,

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.150
Ukraine branded Chinese maker Geely

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:34.260
as a sponsor of war for
continuing operations in Russia.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.750
- Companies like Geely
have multiple brands

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.540
and some of these brands
are trying to explore

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.250
the Western European market.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.640
So if they make a big push in Russia,

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.580
then it may cause them other problems

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.920
in terms of real political risks

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.740
because it may not be well regarded

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:56.190
in front of Western European consumers.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.480
- [Narrator] Geely declined to comment

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:01.050
on the challenges related
to its operations in Russia.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.430
Russia's after door plants,

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:05.010
which now produces Chinese passenger cars,

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.263
didn't respond to a request for comments.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:12.000
Chinese automakers expansion
into the Russian market

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.680
highlights the ever closer ties
between Beijing and Moscow.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.720
At the moment, the relationship appears

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.760
to be mutually beneficial.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.430
However, the question is
whether Chinese brands

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.300
are willing to keep taking the
risks associated with Russia

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.460
and manage the unpredictable nature

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.208
of doing business there in the long run.

00:04:32.208 --> 00:04:34.708
(tense music)

